# New, unproven shape — test drive, not a construction.
#
# Proves NewUnprovenShapeShape, a shape whose entire decision (is this new,
# is it proven) is computed by SPARQL alone -- no Python set-difference or
# pass/fail logic anywhere. A loader's only real job is asserting
# declaredInSnapshot; this fixture proves the rule reads that data correctly.
#
# Sh_NewNoProof: declared only in Current, no provenByFixture -> fires.
# Sh_NewWithProof: declared only in Current, has provenByFixture -> silent.
# Sh_Existing: declared in both Current and Baseline -> silent, whether or
#   not it has provenByFixture (an already-published shape is grandfathered).

@prefix backlog: <http://example.org/backlog#> .
@prefix sh:      <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#> .
@prefix ex:      <http://example.org/newshapetest#> .

ex:Sh_NewNoProof a sh:NodeShape ; backlog:declaredInSnapshot backlog:Snapshot_Current .

ex:Sh_NewWithProof a sh:NodeShape ; backlog:declaredInSnapshot backlog:Snapshot_Current ;
    backlog:provenByFixture "fixture-only: this shape has a real test" .

ex:Sh_Existing a sh:NodeShape ; backlog:declaredInSnapshot backlog:Snapshot_Current ,
    backlog:Snapshot_Baseline .

# v1.1.0 (2026-09-07) -- expected polarity declared on the fixture itself (TBox v1.82.0
# dropped the AdoptionProfile-only domain): Negative, because it exists to make the shape(s) named in its header FIRE; a run of it with no violation would mean that clause no longer fires (Polarity_Negative's own definition).
# Until now the gate inferred 'expected pass' from this filename and had no way to be right.
<http://example.org/newshapetest#> backlog:hasExpectedPolarity backlog:Polarity_Negative .
